Subsequent to my email, I realized you can simply drop the "where" argument entirely. The default to the "where" argument will actually correctly determine the namespace of the package and will put the resulting nimbleFunctions in that namespace.

If you drop the 'where',  I believe roxygenize will work out of the box.  I tried it on my machine and it created the Rd files without a hitch. Let us know if it doesn't work for you.

Chris

